<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Cenbank sets new weaker reais trade level.</title>
<headline>Brazil Cenbank sets new weaker reais trade level.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Central Bank signaled a new weaker trading level for the reais currency by buying dollars at 1.0505 reais and selling dollars at 1.0555 reais in a buy/sell tender in the commercial foreign exchange market, dealers said.</p>
<p>Under the previous mini-band set on February 18, the reais was traded between 1.0500 and 1.0550 per dollar.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo Newsroom, 55-11-2485418))</p>
